  "note": "The A/B pair to 2026-08-17-ingame-full-hipoly-fleet-sweep.json: the SAME pak, the same in-game capped surface, the user, minutes later, with ?benchcar=caddy - every bench road car pinned to the lightest .osm in the fleet (caddy 2.2 MB against sentinel 44 MB / banshee 39 MB; ALL 143 car slots of this build are mod cars, so a stock low-poly pin does not exist). Asked: is the 2.5-3.3x GPU-pass regression the fleet or the world?",
  "analysis": "ANSWER: mostly the WORLD. Pinning the fleet to caddy takes triangles back most of the way toward the 08-09 baseline (ls-noon 3.91M->3.05M vs 2.31M base; ganton 3.14M->2.11M vs 1.57M) and draws too (ganton-noon 1898->1163 vs 1264 base) - but gpu.pass gives back only ~1 ms where cars stand (ls-noon 6.9->5.6, ganton-noon 10.4->9.1, lv-night 11.8->10.8, strip-noon 7.3->6.2) and NOTHING where they do not (country-dusk 12.4->12.0 with 4 cars; ganton-night 10.8->11.4, noise). Against the 08-09 baseline pass is still x2.1-3.6 with the cheap fleet. The fleet's share of the regression is ~10-15 % on car-heavy scenes and ~0 on country-dusk; the rest is what the map draws now. Candidates, in the order the record suggests: (1) the RUNTIME clutter (procobj) - the 08-09 baseline predates the 08-10 per-category ranges and the 08-11 species floor, and country-dusk / ganton are grass scenes; (2) the map content added since 08-09 (Urbanize fold, mods 64/65, LOD/2dfx-at-LOD-range work). NEXT: the same sweep with ?bench=all&benchcar=caddy&procobj=0 (runtime clutter off) - if country-dusk falls back to ~4 ms the clutter density is the cost; then parked=0 / cargen=0 / draw=<smaller> as the remaining runtime dials; only after that a pak-vs-pak comparison. Cost lane = UNCAPPED headless.",
